Kubeapi: This is the primary management component in kubernetes.

When you run the kubectl command it reached to the master node and reaches to the kubeapi(Authenticates and validates) then it retrieves data from ETCD cluster and then again to the kubeapi and kubeapi passes the information to the kubelet in the worker node.

Example: If you need to create a POD or when you give the command to create a POD below is the sequence that takes place.

Authenticate User --> Kubeapi
Validate request --> kubeapi
Retrieve data --> kubeapi
Update ETCD --> ETCD Cluster
scheduled --> Keeps monitor the new POD and Node and send back to the kubeapi
Kubelet --> kubeapi send info to the kubelet to create the POD. Container run time engine deploys the POD and confirm kubelet and kubelet confirms kubeapi

How to install Kubeapi server in master node?

Download it from kubernetes release page
You can check the kubeapi server in below config file

kube-apiserver.service

Kube-apiserver.service file contains lots of configurations which includes the certificates (cacert,key etc.) and these are important.

If you want to install kubeapi server manually you can download it from the kubernetes documentation from the website.
